Rule 1 (a and b must have the same supported dtype: int8/int16/int32/int64/uint8/string)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2) ∧ (dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 2 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 3 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 4 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 11)
>>
Rule 2 (all but the last dimension of a and b must match, with rank ≥ 1)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) ≥ 1 ∧ (if ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 then ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 2] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i))
>>
Rule 3 (validate_indices is a proper boolean flag)
{v_3 : bool} |= v_3 = true ∨ v_3 = false
>>
Rule 4 (when validation is requested, ranks must be consistent and non-zero)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor, v_3 : bool} |= if v_3 then (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ndim(v_1) ≥ 1) else (ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2))
